---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import { link } from '../../lib/links';
import { source } from '../../lib/source';
const rows = [
  {
    id: 'ornith-w2',
    model: 'Ornith 1.5 35B',
    quant: 'Q4_K_M',
    workload: 'W2 · Summarization',
    tokens: '256 / 128',
    normal: '50.27',
    normalNum: 50.27,
    fixed: 'Lookup · 82.19',
    fixedNum: 82.19,
    adaptive: '80.08–80.84',
    adaptiveNum: 80.84,
    maxScale: 90,
    note: 'Favorable input/output overlap. Fixed lookup is faster in the reported results.',
    section: '§8.3 A',
  },
  {
    id: 'ornith-w7',
    model: 'Ornith 1.5 35B',
    quant: 'Q4_K_M',
    workload: 'W7 · Creative prose',
    tokens: '256 / 128',
    normal: '49.75',
    normalNum: 49.75,
    fixed: 'Lookup · 48.84',
    fixedNum: 48.84,
    adaptive: '49.10–49.18',
    adaptiveNum: 49.18,
    maxScale: 90,
    note: 'Adaptive remains below normal. Fallback does not guarantee zero regression.',
    section: '§8.3 A',
  },
  {
    id: 'qwen-w3',
    model: 'Qwen3.8-Flash-Next',
    quant: 'UD-IQ4_XS',
    workload: 'W3 · JSON schema',
    tokens: '256 / 64',
    normal: '18.33',
    normalNum: 18.33,
    fixed: 'MTP · 23.43',
    fixedNum: 23.43,
    adaptive: '23.52',
    adaptiveNum: 23.52,
    maxScale: 40,
    note: 'Development result; the small difference from fixed MTP is not a demonstrated statistically significant win.',
    section: '§8.3 B',
  },
  {
    id: 'qwen-w8',
    model: 'Qwen3.8-Flash-Next',
    quant: 'UD-IQ4_XS',
    workload: 'W8 · Mathematical reasoning',
    tokens: '256 / 64',
    normal: '18.40',
    normalNum: 18.4,
    fixed: 'MTP · 23.94',
    fixedNum: 23.94,
    adaptive: '23.68',
    adaptiveNum: 23.68,
    maxScale: 40,
    note: 'Phase 6.6 adaptive was 24.31 tok/s. This Phase 6.6.1 result regresses versus that revision and fixed MTP.',
    section: '§8.3 B',
  },
];
const fixedLabel = (r: (typeof rows)[number]) => r.fixed.split(' · ')[0];
const fixedValue = (r: (typeof rows)[number]) => r.fixed.split(' · ')[1];
const best = (r: (typeof rows)[number]) =>
  Math.max(r.normalNum, r.fixedNum, r.adaptiveNum) === r.adaptiveNum
    ? 'adaptive'
    : Math.max(r.normalNum, r.fixedNum) === r.fixedNum
      ? 'fixed'
      : 'normal';
---

<Site
  current="performance"
  path="performance/"
  title="Guild performance: the measurement and its limits"
  description="Selected Phase 6.6.1 measurements on dual Xeon Gold 6130 and GTX 1070, with workload, quantization, baseline and explicit limitations."
>
  <div class="page">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="head__meta">Evidence · Phase 6.6.1 · decode tokens per second</p>
      <h1>The measurement, and its limits.</h1>
      <p class="head__lede">
        Selected reported results, not a universal speed claim. Every row belongs to a specific
        model, workload and decoding configuration.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="machine" aria-labelledby="machine">
      <div class="panel">
        <h2 id="machine">A large-RAM server with an 8 GiB card.</h2>
        <dl class="labels">
          <div><dt>CPU</dt><dd>2× Xeon Gold 6130, 32 cores, 64 threads</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Memory</dt><dd>376 GiB DDR4, two NUMA nodes</dd></div>
          <div><dt>GPU</dt><dd>GeForce GTX 1070, 8 GiB</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>Linux, AVX-512 capable</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Reading these results</h2>
        <p>
          Source: Phase 6.6.1 tables in the report snapshot at <code>140f6f7</code>. Engine change
          <code>c7c8c79</code>; earlier Phase 6.6: <code>ed7a5db</code>. GEXEC active, CPU expert
          path, max draft 4, greedy generation. Qwen cross-window parity runs use
          <code>GUILD_IQ_MT_MIN=1</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          These are decode tokens per second, not end-to-end request throughput. Ranges combine
          reported development runs and revisions; they are not confidence intervals or paired
          median and dispersion estimates.
        </p>
        <p>
          GEXEC artifacts were regenerated during tuning. Exact per-row calibration identity is not
          established here, which limits controlled cross-revision comparisons.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="results">
      <h2 id="results">The workload changes the outcome.</h2>
      <div
        class="table-scroll"
        tabindex="0"
        role="region"
        aria-label="Benchmark results; scroll horizontally on small screens"
      >
        <table>
          <caption class="visually-hidden">
            Phase 6.6.1, decode tokens per second, prompt and generated token counts
          </caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Model, quantization</th>
              <th scope="col">Workload</th>
              <th scope="col">Prompt / gen</th>
              <th scope="col">Normal</th>
              <th scope="col">Fixed strategy</th>
              <th scope="col">Adaptive</th>
              <th scope="col">Source</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              rows.map((r) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>
                    {r.model}
                    <br />
                    <code>{r.quant}</code>
                  </td>
                  <td>{r.workload}</td>
                  <td>{r.tokens}</td>
                  <td>{r.normal}</td>
                  <td>{r.fixed}</td>
                  <td>{r.adaptive}</td>
                  <td>
                    <a
                      href={source(
                        'docs/performance/PHASE66_ADAPTIVE_SPECULATIVE_DECODING.md',
                        '#83-controlled-phase-66-vs-phase-661-benchmark-comparison',
                      )}
                    >
                      {r.section} ↗
                    </a>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="runs">
        {
          rows.map((r) => (
            <article class="run">
              <h3>
                {r.model}, {r.workload}
              </h3>
              <p class="run__meta">
                {r.quant} · prompt / gen {r.tokens} · tok/s, scale 0 to {r.maxScale}
              </p>
              <dl class="bars">
                <div>
                  <dt>Normal</dt>
                  <dd class={`bar${best(r) === 'normal' ? ' bar--best' : ''}`} aria-hidden="true">
                    <i style={`--v:${(r.normalNum / r.maxScale).toFixed(4)}`} />
                  </dd>
                  <dd>{r.normal}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Fixed, {fixedLabel(r)}</dt>
                  <dd class={`bar${best(r) === 'fixed' ? ' bar--best' : ''}`} aria-hidden="true">
                    <i style={`--v:${(r.fixedNum / r.maxScale).toFixed(4)}`} />
                  </dd>
                  <dd>{fixedValue(r)}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Adaptive</dt>
                  <dd class={`bar${best(r) === 'adaptive' ? ' bar--best' : ''}`} aria-hidden="true">
                    <i style={`--v:${(r.adaptiveNum / r.maxScale).toFixed(4)}`} />
                  </dd>
                  <dd>{r.adaptive}</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
              <p>{r.note}</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="note note--warn">
        <strong>Held-out counterexample.</strong> Ornith H4 (Riemann tensor) reports 50.16 tok/s normal,
        42.07 fixed lookup and 47.92 adaptive. Adaptive is below normal by about 4.5%. The summary table
        does not provide complete per-run configuration; treat it as a reported observation rather than
        a reproducible paired estimate.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section limits" aria-labelledby="limits">
      <h2 id="limits">What these numbers do not establish.</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          80+ tok/s Ornith results rely on favorable speculative workloads with substantial reusable
          text. They are not general chat throughput, all-model performance, or measurements on a
          small-RAM consumer desktop.
        </p>
        <p>
          Offline calibration measures CPU dispatch and lookup and retrieval microbenchmarks. Full
          verification curves, GPU and context costs, and concurrent-session scaling still include
          estimates. A doubled CPU job count is not a concurrent-session benchmark.
        </p>
        <p>
          The website does not assert successful Phase 6.6.1 sanitizer, complete CUDA CTest,
          seeded-sampling or concurrency validation without retained evidence. The engine report is
          available as a historical source, with those limits noted.
        </p>
        <p>Ryzen 5 5600X / RTX 5070 results remain pending actual hardware measurement.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="archive">
      <h2 id="archive">Read the engineering.</h2>
      <ul class="archive">
        {
          [
            ['phase6', 'Phase 6', 'Populated context, KV placement and reference comparisons.'],
            ['phase65', 'Phase 6.5', 'CPU expert kernels, prefill and end-to-end optimization.'],
            [
              'phase66',
              'Phase 6.6 and 6.6.1',
              'Adaptive decoding, calibration, reported workloads and held-out cases.',
            ],
          ].map(([slug, title, text]) => (
            <li>
              <a href={link('docs', `${slug}/`)}>
                <b>{title}</b>
                <span>{text}</span>
                <em>Read the complete source</em>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Site>
